1. Introduction
   At the beginning of this project, I spent a considerable amount of time searching for reliable resources to study university-level mathematics. Although I found several high-quality materials, many of them required paid subscriptions that were too expensive for a high school student. Fortunately, ChatGPT introduced me to two excellent resources: National Taiwan University OpenCourseWare (NTU OCW),  and the National Academy for Educational Research (NAER).
   I primarily use NAER to look up specialized terminology in both Chinese and English. This has been extremely helpful when preparing my study plan and writing this article. NTU OCW provides free university-level mathematics lectures so I use it as my main learning resource. The course I am studying is Engineering Mathematics taught by professor I-Fan Lin (林以凡). 
